pe over every tag = lua.h's codes), the noreturn raisers, TValue's layout, sentinel tags from their initializers, FFH_RES/FFH_RETRY, first-class tags from lua_type, builtins from cartograph.cjs.BUILTINS; interprocedural summaries keyed by the call's arguments and the path's tags (checkopt(L,4,-1) ≠ checkopt(L,5,1)); LOOPS WITHOUT UNROLLING: each body is a fixpoint over its executable graph (`cfg.graph`) in reverse postorder — a node joins within a loop token, a loop head keeps up to 8 distinct states then WIDENS; goto / break / continue / fall-through are edges, nothing is dropped. The STACK is a value of the path: L->top / L->base move (lua_settop's fill loop), a reallocated stack keeps its indices (the origin is wherever L->stack points), a `lua_State *` is THE thread only when handed it (a finalizer runs on the main one); a callee whose closure never reads the stack is keyed without it, one handed no L and nothing per-element runs ONCE for every element. ⚠ a recursive call is an optimistic guess (CART-1243). The GATE reproduces leaf 1's checker table with no name read. MEASURED 2026-09-30 at fbb36bb6: readings 33 s (a per-tag walk took 492 s, the unrolling walker 40 s with 60 positions dropped — now 0 dropped, 0 over budget, every other reading identical); gate 22 of 27 the same, 5 FINER (a coercion made by a call — checkint's numeric strings —, FFI rejecting thread/proto, checktabornil's nil-but-not-absent); join with leaf 1 42 agree / 13 disagree in 4 causes, every one the path reading's refinement and confirmed by the running LuaJIT; 90 positions only this reading types, witnessed 90 confirmed / 0 contradicted; result counts exact for 87 of 125 functions. CART-1240 leaves 2–3 |\n"}},"decisions":[],"verb":"edit","id":"1790786946.498319-edit"},{"bytes":602,"decided_by":"tactic","invocation":{"touched":[".claude/skills/cartograph/references/questions.md"],"verb":"edit","args":{"file":".claude/skills/cartograph/references/questions.md","before":"| One multi-clause